<H1>Medium data</H1>
Search for medium no. = [1102].
<HR>
Unless otherwise stated, sterilize media by autoclaving at 121&#176;C for 15 min.
<HR>
<P><B><FONT SIZE=3>1102&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;ANAEROBIC NATURAL SEAWATER MEDIUM</FONT></B></P>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Tryptone                                                </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;5.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Yeast extract                                           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;1.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> g  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Resazurin                                               </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;0.5&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> mg  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Natural seawater (filtrated)                         </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;750.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> Distilled water                                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;250.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Mix components thoroughly and adjust pH to 7.0.  Bring to a boil and cool down under a N<sub>2</sub> gas atmosphere.  Distribute the medium in culture vessels (e.g., 10 ml in Balch tubes) under N<sub>2</sub>, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  After cooling, aseptically and anaerobically add per liter the following solutions (autoclaved and stored under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere):  <br>
<TABLE BORDER>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% L-Cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O solution           </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;6.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
<TR><TD WIDTH=75%> 5% Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution                       </TD><TD WIDTH=15% ALIGN=RIGHT><font size=+1><tt>&nbsp;6.0&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</tt></font></TD><TD WIDTH=10% ALIGN=RIGHT> ml  </TD></TR>
</TABLE>
Comment: For strain JCM 32399, supplement with 10 mM sodium pyruvate.  For JCM 33129, omit resazurin and the reducing agents (L-cysteine&#183;HCl&#183;H<sub>2</sub>O and Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O).  For JCM 33131, supplement with 10 ml/L trace vitamins (see Medium No. <a href="/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197">197</a>).       <br>
